01:07:41,538 --> 01:07:47,538
The Assassination of Jesse James by the Coward Robert Ford is a 2007 American epic
revisionist Western film written and directed by Andrew Dominik.

12
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
Based on Ron Hansen's 1983 novel of the same name, the film dramatizes the relationship between Jesse
James and Robert Ford, focusing on the events that lead up to the titular killing.

13
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It stars Brad Pitt as James and Casey Affleck as Ford, with Sam Shepard, Mary-Louise Parker, Paul
Schneider, Jeremy Renner, Zooey Deschanel, and Sam Rockwell in supporting roles.

14
01:26:09,230 --> 01:26:15,230
Photography started on August 29, 2005, and ended in December 2005.

15
01:32:18,461 --> 01:32:24,461
Filming took place near Calgary, Canmore, and
Edmonton, Alberta, and Winnipeg, Manitoba.

16
01:38:27,692 --> 01:38:33,692
To achieve the visual style he wanted for the movie, Dominik took influences from many sources, including still
photographers, images clipped from magazines, stills from Days of Heaven, and even Polaroids.

17
01:44:36,923 --> 01:44:42,923
The original edit of the movie was envisioned by Dominik to be "a dark, contemplative
examination of fame and infamy", reaching more than three hours in runtime.

18
01:50:46,153 --> 01:50:52,153
This was opposed by the studio and the film was edited repeatedly.

19
01:56:55,384 --> 01:57:01,384
The Assassination of Jesse James by the Coward Robert Ford had its world premiere at the 64th Venice International Film Festival
on September 2, 2007, and was theatrically released in the United States on September 21, 2007, by Warner Bros.

20
02:03:04,615 --> 02:03:10,615
The film received positive reviews from critics, who particularly praised Pitt and Affleck's performances and
Roger Deakins' cinematography, but was criticized for its long runtime and was a box-office bomb.

21
02:09:13,846 --> 02:09:19,846
At the 80th Academy Awards, it earned two nominations: Best Supporting
Actor for Affleck and Best Cinematography for Deakins.

22
02:15:23,076 --> 02:15:29,076
Affleck was also nominated for a Golden Globe, a Screen Actors Guild Award, and a Critics'
Choice Award for Best Supporting Actor, while Pitt won the Volpi Cup for Best Actor.

23
02:21:32,307 --> 02:21:38,307
It has since gained a large fan following, with many of them organizing
re-releases of the film under the "Jesse James Revival" banner.

24
02:27:41,538 --> 02:27:47,538
The film explores themes of media, killing,
missouri, admiration, hold-up robbery.

25
02:33:50,769 --> 02:33:56,769
The tone is emotional.
